@startuml
title 9. Proximity unlock (measured fix -> server grant)
autonumber
actor User
participant "Geolocation" as GPS
participant Client
participant Gateway
participant Spatial
participant Auth
database SpatialDB

User -> Client : walking
GPS -> Client : watchPosition fix (lat, lon, accuracy, timestamp)
Client -> Client : evaluate the MEASURED fix only\n(accuracy finite and > 0; if proximity required:\naccuracy <= 100 and distance < 50 m;\nskip known and in-flight POIs)
alt no candidates, or this fix was already sent
    Client -> Client : nothing sent
else candidates (max 50, nearest first)
    Client -> Gateway : POST /api/spatial/locations/unlock\n{lat, lon, accuracyMeters, osmIds[]} (Bearer)
    Gateway -> Gateway : validate JWT, set X-User-Id
    Gateway -> Spatial : forward (StripPrefix=2)
    Spatial -> Spatial : validate boundary (ranges, accuracy, 1..50 ids)
    Spatial -> Auth : GET /settings (X-User-Id, 1 s budget)
    Auth --> Spatial : 200 { requireProximity }
    note right of Spatial : fail-closed: timeout, 4xx/5xx, empty or\nunreadable payload => requireProximity = true
    alt requireProximity and accuracyMeters > 100
        Spatial --> Client : 422 (whole request, nothing written)
    else
        Spatial -> SpatialDB : one statement: INSERT poi_unlock\nSELECT FROM location_point WHERE osm_id = ANY(?)\nAND (exempt OR ST_DWithin(geom, point, 50))\nON CONFLICT (user_id, osm_id) DO UPDATE (no-op)\nRETURNING + UNION already-unlocked rows of this user
        SpatialDB --> Spatial : osm_ids unlocked for this user
        Spatial --> Client : 200 { unlocked[], refused[] }
    end
    Client -> Client : add to known-unlocked, release in-flight ids
end
note right of Client : refused is normal (edge of the radius, unknown id).\nNo retry in place; the next measured fix may send again.
@enduml
